      "reveal": "<span lang=\"de\">-ig</span> ~ -y in English, as we noted when we were puzzling out weather words! Adverbs and adjectives have the same form in German, except that adjectives change to agree with nouns, for example in <span lang=\"de\">eine neblige Nacht</span> \"a foggy night\". Did you also notice that some words changed form when the suffix was added? <span lang=\"de\">Nebel</span> \"fog\" became <span lang=\"de\">nebl-ig</span>, losing an <span lang=\"de\">e</span>. By the way, this word has the same source as our word \"nebula\"!"
