      "reveal": "<span lang=\"de\">-los</span> ~ \"-less\" and <span lang=\"de\">-voll</span> ~ \"-full\", as you've doubtless worked out! Rather than losing letters as with other prefixes, here we're adding a linking <span lang=\"de\">-s-</span> on occasion.\n\nHere's another fun <span lang=\"de\">-los</span> word: <span lang=\"de\">zweifellos</span> \"doubtless\". Breaking the <span lang=\"de\">Zweifel</span> \"doubt\" part down more, it means something like \"in two minds\" (<span lang=\"de\">zwei</span> ~ \"two\"). The English word \"doubt\" also shows the same connection between doubt and duality — it shares a root with \"double\", via Latin."
